<attribute name="version" nodeId="3e394abf"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="4c4a8777">&lt;p&gt;
    To organize and define an organization&apos;s purpose, mission, vision, strategy, brand, values, and purpose pillars, EY
    recommends the use of Corporate DNA. Using the Corporate DNA structure, organizations can differentiate each of the
    elements and link them together in a cohesive manner.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Corporate DNA creates a picture of why an organization exists, focusing on what benefit it brings to others
    (&lt;em&gt;purpose&lt;/em&gt;), what it exists to do (&lt;em&gt;mission&lt;/em&gt;), what it stands for (&lt;em&gt;values&lt;/em&gt;) and how it
    communicates these to the market (&lt;em&gt;brand&lt;/em&gt;). A clear &lt;em&gt;vision&lt;/em&gt; for the future with a path of how to get
    there (&lt;em&gt;strategy&lt;/em&gt;) is established. Corporate DNA also operationalizes an organization&apos;s purpose through
    &quot;&lt;em&gt;purpose pillars&lt;/em&gt;&quot;, which is a set of behaviors of how a organization conducts itself when &quot;it&apos;s at its best&quot;
    and the impact of those behaviors on stakeholders.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table title=&quot;&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; width=&quot;85%&quot; border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Element
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Definition
            &lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Purpose
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                What an organization is doing for someone else. The &quot;philosophical heartbeat” of the company.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Mission
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                An explicit declaration of the charge or job to be done by an organization. The mission statement clarifies
                what business the organization is in, and by implication what business or businesses it is not in.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Vision
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;
                    An envisioned future state that an organization aspires to and actively seeks to reach through its
                    strategies and actions. A vision communicates a mental picture of the long-term ambition of the
                    enterprise.
                &lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Strategy
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                The long-term (3-5 year), broad, overarching approach to accomplish the vision or a goals of an
                organization.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Values
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                The shared set of beliefs held by the organization that influence and guide the behaviors and decisions of
                its members.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Purpose Pillars
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                A set of attributes of how the organization conducts itself when &quot;it&apos;s at its best.&quot; Every pillar directly
                relates to a value of the organization and suggests behaviors and the impact and stakeholder benefits of
                those behaviors.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Brand
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                The collection icons, visuals, messaging and or taglines associated with an organization, product, service
                or inititive.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../core.bus.common.base/guidances/concepts/./resources/corp_dna_concept.png&quot; width=&quot;890&quot; height=&quot;408&quot; /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;em&gt;EY&apos;s Corporate DNA and Purpose Story (Purpose Pillars not shown)&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
